# Executive Summary: Two-Way SMS Reminder Test

**For:** Director of Ambulatory Access (simulated 24-clinic outpatient network)
**Data:** synthetic, generated by `src/generate_data.py` (seed 42). All figures describe a simulated network.

## Recommendation: {decision}

The test met the rule we wrote down before it started. Unfilled slots fell, the 95% confidence interval excludes zero, and estimated net value stays positive at the low end of its range.

## What happened (17 weeks, 2025-03-03 to 2025-06-29, about {n_real} slot appointments per arm)

| | One-way SMS (today) | Two-way SMS | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| No-show rate | {ns_c}% | {ns_t}% | {ns_d} pp ({ns_rel}% relative) |
| Late cancellations (< 24 h) | {lc_c}% | {lc_t}% | {lc_d} pp |
| Late-cancelled slots refilled | {rf_c}% | {rf_t}% | {rf_d} pp |
| **Slots left empty** | **{unf_c}%** | **{unf_t}%** | **{unf_d} pp** |

- **Late cancellations went up, and that is the intended effect.** Patients who used to no-show now cancel a day or more ahead, and the clinic can refill the slot. The empty-slot rate is the number that tracks revenue and access.
- **Medicaid patients benefit most** ({medicaid_d} pp on no-shows). Commercial patients still benefit ({commercial_d} pp).

## Value (simulated economics)

| Option | Slots recovered per year | Net value per year (95% range) |
|---|---|---|
| Network-wide | {full_slots} | {full_net} ({full_lo} to {full_hi}) |
| Medicaid + self-pay only | {tgt_slots} | {tgt_net} ({tgt_lo} to {tgt_hi}) |

Assumptions: $0.04 per text, $18,000 per year platform fee, $160 margin per filled slot. Network-wide costs {full_cost} per year and adds about {incr_full} more than the targeted option. The margin is an upper bound if a clinic has no waitlist to refill from.

## One data problem we caught

One clinic ({srm_clinic}) lost its treatment-group records from {srm_from} to {srm_to} because of a logging outage. The overall 50/50 check did not show it. A clinic-by-week check did, and the text-message log confirmed it. We removed that clinic-window from both groups before computing results.

## Next steps

1. Proceed ({decision}). Keep a 5% holdout for one quarter to confirm the effect holds.
2. Add the empty-slot rate to the access scorecard next to the no-show rate.
3. Add an automatic per-clinic daily check to the experiment platform.
